<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2474" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱμό-ρροος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱμό-ρρους</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ουν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>flowing with blood</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρώματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Art.</u>
					69
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ. φλέβες</span> veins so large
				<i>as to cause a haemorrhage</i> if wounded, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				11
			</span></i>, ubiv.<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>suffering from haemorrhoids</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				4.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
				Subst., a serpent, whose bite makes <i>blood
			flow</i> from all parts of the body, <i><span class="en">
				Philum.
				<u>Ven.</u>
				21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				282
			</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱμορροΐς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					111
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
